id: pm-github-o9r7
title: Explain scheduled install mismatches and preserve redacted command failure diagnostics
description: "The November 6 fleet watch still samples old workflow releases with silent exact-version verification failures and hidden closeout stderr. Existing normalization, pagination and no-op fixes require caller pin adoption. Strengthen the current workflow install verifier with actionable safe messages, preserve actionable non-JSON or host-wrapped error details through the diagnostic path, and record the per-caller adoption and validation inventory without changing caller repositories."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: changelog-unreleased,closeout,diagnostics,sync,workflows
created_at: "2026-11-06T22:47:15.345Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T08:49:00.891Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T08:49:00.815Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-14T08:49:00.815Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Real workflow regressions fail under function-only behavioral reversions; version mismatches identify safe expected and actual versions; command errors remain actionable after privacy redaction; existing gates still refuse publication; public caller replays distinguish package fixes from caller-owned policy and provenance.
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T22:48:41.447Z",codex-agent,"REST evidence distinguishes old release adoption from current defects: padded tag verification silently exits after a healthy install; old repeated imports stamp updated_at; old closeout hides its actual failure. Existing main already normalizes tags and avoids repeated writes. This item adds safe install mismatch diagnostics and hardens failure receipt decoding, with executable workflow tests and the caller follow-up matrix on pm-github-samq."
  "2026-11-06T22:56:57.243Z",codex-agent,"The exact pm-slack run-head replay reproduces the old failure using its pinned SDK 2026.11.4 and pm-github 2026.10.28: the second identical import updates one item and changes its item/history files. Published pm-github 2026.11.4 with that same SDK returns updated=0, unchanged=true and zero changed durable files. All issue/comment/timeline inputs came from REST-only public snapshots; optional GraphQL closure enrichment was not queried. The old closeout dry-run exits 1 with Unverifiable GitHub pagination. A latest-version full CLI preview reached the scratch deadline; it is not counted as passing."
  "2026-11-06T23:00:43.810Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs ran in a disposable repository copy. Reverting only the installed-version verifier in both reusable workflows fails 2/2 metadata-diagnostic regressions. Restoring only the prior stderr decoder fails 2/2 plain-stderr regressions. Replacing only diagnostic redaction with the previous identity behavior fails 2/2 privacy regressions. Restoring all fixes passes 5/5 selected tests, with zero skips or cancellations. Production and test typechecks and ESLint also pass. A workflow integration probe initially packed without a build and correctly refused the missing entry; the rebuilt probe is being rerun."
  "2026-11-06T23:05:39.176Z",codex-agent,"Final focused validation: 81/81 complete self-versioned-workflow and scheduled-refusal tests pass; the rebuilt packed CLI workflow reporter integration passes 1/1; the linked pm test selection passes 5/5. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, existing Git-object identity/privacy gate and publish-attestation checks pass. A recorded REST pagination-only replay fails with installed 2026.10.28 and completes with installed 2026.11.4; full latest live closeout is not certified because of the read deadline/budget. All eleven generic-closeout callers currently expose numeric next-page REST links. The secondary preview-validation limitation is tracked separately on pm-github-xgk0. Full npm/Bun release and coverage gates remain for PR CI as authorized."
  "2026-11-07T06:54:19.766Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR #225 after review and merged current main before edits. Class rules: live operational entry points must reference current complete evidence; mismatch contracts must assert both version operands; every rejected metadata fixture must remain absent from output; generic transport/host errors must not hide more specific causes or structured receipts; redaction must use original-source start/end spans, never decoded lengths. Auditing all scanner consumers, workflow reporters, README/tracker entry points, CLI formats and packed Node/Bun paths. Own claims reacquired; original investigation and caller replays will not be repeated. Full npm and Bun gates are required for this review round."
  "2026-11-07T07:02:23.882Z",codex-agent,"All five review findings are valid and fixed at the class level. Searches covered both reusable install verifiers, all scanner consumers and hit constructors, the shared sync/closeout diagnostic command, live README/tracker entry points, and existing JSON/TOON and packed-consumer paths. Focused acceptance passes 130/130, including one actual packed artifact consumed by npm and native Bun in JSON and TOON on a non-git tracker. Focused workflow-diagnostic coverage is 100/100/100/100. Revert controls in a disposable copy: reverting README or the adoption description independently fails 1/1 each; omitting only the expected version fails 2/2; leaking only malformed metadata fails 2/2; reverting only the decoder, receipt selection, redactor or scanner source-span function independently fails 1/1 each. Full restoration passes 7/7. No existing assertion or policy gate was weakened; the encoded-content test now requires complete masking while preserving safe surrounding context."
  "2026-11-07T07:09:46.801Z",codex-agent,"The class audit also found the symmetric precedence edge: a failed stdout report with no actionable rows could override specific stderr. Both directions now prefer actionable content, including generic wrappers with repeated publication suffixes, blank host sections and case-varied error prefixes. An incomplete full-gate attempt was stopped to add that regression and is not counted as passing. The final pure class tests and all eight independent revert controls were rerun; each control fails and the restored selection passes 7/7. Source is frozen for the restarted serial full npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-11-07T08:26:02.746Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm gate passed: npm run release:check exited 0 after 4451.22 seconds. Tests: 1782 total, 1780 passed, zero failures/cancellations, two existing pm-cli#1656 compensation skips. The skips remain missing lifecycle-compensation evidence, not passing behavior. All 30 authored modules measured exact 100/100/100/100: 14415/14415 lines and statements, 456/456 functions, 5440/5440 branches. Audit, pack dry-run, changelog and publication attestation also passed. Npm coverage receipts were preserved before the serial Bun gate started. The extra canonical-ownership correction has its own disposable data-revert proof: restoring this follow-up's duplicate tag fails 1/1; restoring the corrected data passes 1/1."
  "2026-11-07T09:22:36.554Z",codex-agent,"Review round complete: all five findings are addressed at their shared class boundaries. Serial isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0; durations 4451.22 and 3448.48 seconds. Each suite: 1782 tests, 1780 passes, zero failures/cancellations, two unchanged pm-cli#1656 lifecycle-compensation skips. Each gate: all 30 authored modules, 14415/14415 lines and statements, 456/456 functions, 5440/5440 branches; exact 100 percent in all four dimensions. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, Git identity/privacy, audit (zero production vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog and attestation passed. All nine independent revert controls fail as documented; restored selection passes 7/7, restored provenance passes 1/1, and the final linked regression selection passes 8/8. Both full-gate commands are linked, and the focused selection was executed through pm test --run --progress. No existing tests, skips or policy thresholds were weakened. Current main is merged; runtime source remained unchanged throughout the completed full gates. Full latest live closeout and scheduled-token acceptance remain unverified boundaries. Releasing only my own claims; items remain in progress for orchestrator verification."
